  "goodToKnow": "Die Herrin is the female form of der Herr in the sense of master or ruler: die Herrin des Hauses, die Herrin über ihr eigenes Leben. Herr or Herrin der Lage sein means to be in control of the situation. Dog owners are affectionately called Herrchen and Frauchen: Wo ist dein Herrchen? Herrin can sound old-fashioned or have other connotations, so in everyday speech the owner is die Besitzerin. Plural: die Herrinnen."
